{"content":[{"c":["UZ (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Aram’s firstborn son and a descendant of Shem (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.23","r":"Gen.10.23","rawR":"Gen.10.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.23","value":"Gen.10.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:23"},"). In the parallel passage in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.17","r":"1Chr.1.17","rawR":"1Chr.1.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.17","value":"1Chr.1.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 1:17"},", Uz is linked directly to Shem without mention of Aram. He is perhaps the forefather of the Aramean nation situated in the Syrian desert regions."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Firstborn son of Abraham’s brother Nahor by his concubine, Milcah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.22.21","r":"Gen.22.21","rawR":"Gen.22.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.22.21","value":"Gen.22.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 22:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Son of Dishan and the grandson of Seir the Horite (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.28","r":"Gen.36.28","rawR":"Gen.36.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.28","value":"Gen.36.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.42","r":"1Chr.1.42","rawR":"1Chr.1.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.42","value":"1Chr.1.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"UzPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.23","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.23","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.23"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 1:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.17"},{"anchorText":"Gn 22:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.22.21","rawQueryVa